# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ClaimGuard AI — repository hygiene
# Note: uv.lock IS committed (it pins the whole environment) — deliberately
# not ignored. .env.example is committed as the template — see the negation
# below.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ----- Python -------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.venv/
venv/
env/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.pyright/
dist/
build/
*.egg-info/
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
htmlcov/
.mutmut-cache/

# ----- uv -----------------------------------------------------------------
.uv/

# ----- Node / Next.js -----------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
.next/
out/
.turbo/
.pnpm-store/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# ----- Secrets (never commit) --------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.jks
*.keystore

# ----- Artifacts / benchmarks ---------------------------------------------
artifacts/
docs/benchmark/*.json

# ----- Mentor-delivered material (reference only, never our source) -------
# The CSTAM-VELODOC starter pack ships its own tooling, formatting and
# SHA256SUMS manifest. It is the grading oracle we run locally; it is not part
# of our product source, so it is not tracked and not linted/typed.
ClaimGuardAI_Student_Starter_Pack/
ClaimGuardAI_Student_Starter_Pack.zip

# ----- OS -----------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
*.swp
*~

# ----- IDE / editors ------------------------------------------------------
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json.example
# Local-only planning workspace (retired per-task planning docs)
claimguard-plans-local/

# repowise codebase index (local tool state, ~0.5 MB binary)
.repowise/

# Local-only engineering handoff. Tracked until 2026-09-27; removed from the working
# tree AND from every commit so the team working in this repository cannot read it or
# its history. Keep it local: never `git add -f` it, never paste it into anything the
# team sees. TEAM-TASKS.md and TEAM-ROADMAP.md are the team-visible briefs.
HANDOFF.md

# Private senior operator guide contains synthetic local demo credentials.
# Share it directly with the intended teammate; never force-add it to Git.
SENIOR-TECHNICAL-ADMIN-GUIDE.md

# Local demo credentials. Real values, synthetic accounts: never committed.
examples/demo/CREDENTIALS.local.md

# LaTeX build scratch and the downloaded engine: 110 MB of re-downloadable tooling.
tmp/
reports/**/tectonic-bin/
reports/**/tectonic.zip

# Archify renders each diagram spec into a ~700 KB viewer with the library inlined, and writes a
# visual-check page plus eight screenshots. The report embeds its own copies from `assets/`, so
# only the authored specs under `diagrams/*.json` are source.
reports/**/diagrams/*.html
reports/**/diagrams/*.png
reports/**/diagrams/*.visual-check.json
